  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` passes (8 of 8). I didn't run the new tests against the old queue, so I haven't confirmed they fail without the fix.\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a rejected job never decremented `running`, so its slot stayed taken and the queue stalled. Failures now free the slot, reject only that job's promise, and start the next job. A job that throws synchronously or returns a plain value is now handled the same way.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving too early:** it only checked that nothing was pending. It now also requires that nothing is running.\n- **Only one job after `pause()`/`resume()`:** `resume()` started a single job. The start logic is now a loop that fills every free slot, so concurrency 4 runs four jobs again.\n\nI added six regression tests to `test/queue.test.js`:\n- continuing after a rejected job;\n- a job that throws synchronously, and one that returns a plain value;\n- `onIdle()` waiting for running jobs;\n- `onIdle()` resolving immediately when already idle;\n- `resume()` filling all free slots;\n- `pause()` not interrupting running jobs.",
